      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A cracked well doesn't need refilling—it needs a new shape. But you're not a well anymore. You're the ground beneath it, and you're telling yourself you're dry while rain keeps falling through you. Slumps end; this is something else. It's a quiet death of an old version of you, and that grief is loud. Don't make art yet. Just sit in the shell for a while, and let the clock tick without demanding it mean something. The point isn't to refill—it's to learn what wants to grow in this cracked earth.",
