      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I hear you—and there's a profound honesty in that quiet, in not forcing a story that feels finished. But even silence is part of a story, not its end. If you can't grow right now, then don't. Just exist as the empty page, the held breath. The weight you're carrying isn't a failure—it's the cost of being alive to your own truth. You don't have to pretend there's a next version. Just let this one breathe, even if only barely. You don't have to reach for light today—only to notice you're still here, noticing.",
